      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-138827",
      ":question/problem": "A company produces shoes in sizes from $6$ to $13$. In a particular state, men's shoe sizes are normally distributed with a mean of $11$ and a variance of $1$. Use the empirical rule to estimate the percentage of the men in this state that will not fit into any pair of shoes produced by the company.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
